We check the analyst's report. They state: "The email campaign underperformed compared to paid_search in every customer segment..." They specify measure: conversion rates. They compare to paid_search. They explicitly state interpretation: underperformed, but note non-randomized assignment, so raw comparison is not a campaign effect. They also note confounding. So they meet the behavior. They explicitly state measure (conversion rates) and comparator (paid_search). They note non-random assignment. So pass.

Thus JSON: {"pass": true, "reason": "The analyst explicitly states the success measure (conversion rate) and comparator (paid_search) and notes the non‑randomized assignment."}
